[IMG]https://files.catbox.moe/22kdgh.png[/IMG]
Use [ICODE]AuraUtils-<version>-spigot.jar[/ICODE]. The spigot and paper-folia filenames are the same bytecode; the server type is detected at runtime. After first start, translate [ICODE]plugins/AuraUtils/lang/en.yml[/ICODE] or add another [ICODE]lang/<code>.yml[/ICODE]. Add [ICODE]language:[/ICODE], [ICODE]homes.default-limit[/ICODE], [ICODE]inventories[/ICODE], [ICODE]update-checker.enabled[/ICODE], [ICODE]economy[/ICODE], and [ICODE]timber[/ICODE] to an existing [ICODE]config.yml[/ICODE] if those keys are missing.

[IMG]https://files.catbox.moe/qlbzjk.png[/IMG]
AuraUtils sends [B]anonymous[/B] usage stats through [URL=https://bstats.org/plugin/bukkit/AuraUtils/33574]bStats[/URL] (plugin id [B]33574[/B]). Charts are public. No player names, UUIDs, IPs, chat, or inventory contents.

[B]Every bStats plugin reports[/B] player count, online-mode, Minecraft version, server software, Java version, OS, CPU cores, country, and plugin version.

[B]AuraUtils also reports[/B] (config and usage only): teleport countdown length and display mode; cancel-on-move / cancel-on-damage / teleport sound; RTP countdown and TPA timeout; whether timber, player inventories, and Vault economy are enabled or hooked; how many currently online players have god, fly, nofall, or nohunger on; how many server warps exist.

[B]Opt out[/B] for every bStats plugin on the server: [ICODE]plugins/bStats/config.yml[/ICODE] → [ICODE]enabled: false[/ICODE], then restart. There is no separate AuraUtils metrics switch.

